# Frontend Patterns

## Atomic Design

Organize UI under `apps/web/src/components/`:

| Layer     | Path        | Responsibility                          |
| --------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Atoms     | `atoms/`    | Single UI primitive (Button, Input)     |
| Molecules | `molecules/`| Small composed groups (SearchBar)       |
| Organisms | `organisms/`| Distinct UI sections (Header, CardList) |
| Templates | `templates/`| Page layout without real data           |
| Pages     | `pages/`    | Route-level screens wiring organisms    |

One component per folder:

```
components/atoms/Button/
  Button.tsx
  Button.test.tsx
  index.ts          # re-export only
```

- ✅ Compose up the hierarchy (pages → templates → organisms → …)
- ❌ Atoms importing organisms; cross-layer “shortcuts”

## Tailwind CSS

- **Styling**: Tailwind utilities only; avoid new `.css` per component
- **Global**: `index.css` — `@import "tailwindcss"` / directives only
- ✅ `className="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-4 py-2"`
- ❌ Inline `style={{}}` for layout/theme; ❌ component-scoped CSS files for UI

## Components

- Functional components; named export in file, barrel via `index.ts`
- Props typed with `interface` or `type`; no `any`
- Prefer composition over prop drilling; extract hooks when logic grows

## Tests (mandatory)

Every component **must** have a co-located test covering **essential usage**:

- Renders with required props / default state
- Primary user interaction (click, type, submit) when applicable
- Key accessible output (role, label, text) — use Testing Library queries

```tsx
// ✅ Button.test.tsx — render + click + label
it('calls onClick when pressed', async () => {
  const onClick = vi.fn()
  render(<Button onClick={onClick}>Save</Button>)
  await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }))
  expect(onClick).toHaveBeenCalledOnce()
})
```

- ❌ Ship a new component without its `.test.tsx`
- ❌ Snapshot-only tests with no behavior assertion
